{
  "name": "muse-planner",
  "description": "A read-only pi-subagents child backed by Meta's Muse Code CLI (`muse exec`) on the local Muse login: the parent session calls it by name for a plan or an analysis and returns the text; it never edits the repository. Pi-shaped (pi-subagents), delivered through yolo's `files` kind — inert if pi-subagents is not installed.",
  "contributes": [
    // THE WRAPPER the `muse-planner` agent's runner runs. It lands in `~/.pi/agent/bin`,
    // beside the definition. The agent definition deliberately does NOT invoke it by its bare
    // name: the external-cli runner resolves a bare command on PATH requiring the exec bit
    // (pi-subagents' `resolveBinary` -> `X_OK`), and the EMBEDDED pack channel cannot deliver
    // one — embed.FS reports 0444 for every file whatever its mode on disk, and the
    // materializer writes 0o644 (internal/packload's copyEmbeddedTree). So a bare `command:
    // muse-planner-exec.sh` would work only when the pack is selected BY PATH (packstage
    // carries 0o111) and would silently fail as a SHIPPED pack. The definition therefore
    // invokes `bash -c 'exec "$HOME/.pi/agent/bin/muse-planner-exec.sh"'`: `bash` is always
    // executable, and `-c` lets `$HOME` resolve the path without a shell expanding `~`. The
    // file still ships executable on disk, so a by-path selection can run it directly too.
    //
    // It reads the child's prompt from stdin and hands it to
    // `muse exec --prompt-file` under `--disable-approval` (sandbox kept), a bounded
    // `--max-model-steps` and a per-run `:read-only` permission profile, with its own deadline
    // and the CLI's exit codes propagated. The profile id carries its leading colon (the bare
    // `read-only` resolves to nothing), and the wrapper's `-c` value is JSON, so it is quoted.
    // The file's own header is the reference.
    {
      "from": "files/scripts/muse-planner-exec.sh",
      "into": ".pi/agent/bin/muse-planner-exec.sh",
      "kind": "files"
    },
    // THE AGENT DEFINITION. `~/.pi/agent/agents/` is pi-subagents' user agent directory
    // (`getAgentDir()/agents`; `~/.agents` is the other user scope it also reads). A
    // definition needs `name` and `description` or it is skipped entirely, and `runner` is the
    // block that makes it an external CLI rather than a Pi child. No `adapter`: only a
    // code-owned id (codex-exec, claude-code, cursor-agent and their -writer twins) may set
    // one, and this is the generic one-shot-stdin runner.
    {
      "from": "files/agents/muse-planner.md",
      "into": ".pi/agent/agents/muse-planner.md",
      "kind": "files"
    }
  ]
}
